[[15,1,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/2429584\">7040B10</a></p><p>1. Pull the handle (1a) and move the rear seat (1b) forward.</p><p>2. Undo the bolt.</p><p>3. Remove the preformed element.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2045288.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[15,1,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the preformed element\nis not damaged.</p><p>Position the preformed element and fasten\nit using the bolt.</p><p>Refit the rear seat.</p><p><a href=\"#/2429584\">7040B10</a></p>"]]